Title: Low Orbit
Credit: Written by
Author: Previz Stage
Draft date: 2026-10-24

INT. ORBITAL STATION - CARGO DECK - NIGHT

A long steel deck under cold strip lights. Stacked cargo pods, exposed conduit, a wall of viewport glass showing the curve of the Earth below. A maintenance drone hums along the ceiling rail.

DR. IMANI OKAFOR (40s, tall, close-cropped grey hair, a navy flight suit with a medical patch, magnetic boots) checks a readout on a pod.

TARO (20s, wiry, buzz cut, orange technician coveralls tied at the waist over a black thermal shirt) jogs up the deck toward her.

TARO
The reactor team isn't answering. Any of them.

OKAFOR
How long?

TARO
Eleven minutes. Comms are fine. They just stopped.

OKAFOR
(closing the readout)
Then we go down there ourselves.

EXT. LUNAR LANDING FIELD - DAY

A grey regolith plain under a black sky. Landing pads marked with faded orange lights, a squat habitat module half buried in the dust, the Earth hanging low over the horizon. A small spacecraft lifts off from a far pad on a silent plume.

Okafor and Taro stand at the edge of the pad in pressure suits, helmets on.

OKAFOR
That was our ride.

TARO
It'll come back. It has to come back.

OKAFOR
Nothing has to do anything out here.
